\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {II}{\ignorespaces Fine observations improve forecasts without establishing an acquisition advantage. Results use recorded episode artifacts. B is the original disturbance panel and C the corrective panel. Local MAE one hour ahead is in kWh per affected household, using 80 local episodes in B and 12 in C. {\color {red}\sout {Detection }}{\color {blue}\uwave {Original detection }}and correct group localization use {\color {red}\sout {all }}{\color {blue}\uwave {lags 0--5 for B's }}96 {\color {red}\sout {and 12 }}demand episodes {\color {red}\sout {, respectively. }}{\color {blue}\uwave {and lags 0--6 for C's 12. }}Control alarms use unmodified episodes. Delay includes misses at 3.5 h. Representations receiving identical evidence match their source policy and are omitted as duplicate rows.}}{8}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:results}{{II}{8}{Fine observations improve forecasts without establishing an acquisition advantage. Results use recorded episode artifacts. B is the original disturbance panel and C the corrective panel. Local MAE one hour ahead is in kWh per affected household, using 80 local episodes in B and 12 in C. \DIFdelbeginFL \DIFdelFL {Detection }\DIFdelendFL \DIFaddbeginFL \DIFaddFL {Original detection }\DIFaddendFL and correct group localization use \DIFdelbeginFL \DIFdelFL {all }\DIFdelendFL \DIFaddbeginFL \DIFaddFL {lags 0--5 for B's }\DIFaddendFL 96 \DIFdelbeginFL \DIFdelFL {and 12 }\DIFdelendFL demand episodes \DIFdelbeginFL \DIFdelFL {, respectively. }\DIFdelendFL \DIFaddbeginFL \DIFaddFL {and lags 0--6 for C's 12. }\DIFaddendFL Control alarms use unmodified episodes. Delay includes misses at 3.5 h. Representations receiving identical evidence match their source policy and are omitted as duplicate rows}{table.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Tracing a hidden local change from observations to acquisition. Example b00 uses exact cancellation at nominal magnitude three, selected by first background and fixed family and magnitude before comparison. Gray shading marks the disturbance. (a) Regional demand on observed support varies with the real background, while the injected change sums to zero in every group. (b) Positive and negative meter sets change locally. (c) Forecasts one hour ahead share target times and observed support, without assuming foreknowledge. (d) Affected probes change scores without crossing the acquisition gate during the event. The {\color {blue}\uwave {annotated }}later {\color {red}\sout {trigger }}{\color {blue}\uwave {spike occurs after the disturbance and }}also appears on the paired unmodified background. Acquisition remains unchanged and localization is missed. Local sets are evaluator labels unavailable to the policy.}}{8}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:episode}{{2}{8}{Tracing a hidden local change from observations to acquisition. Example b00 uses exact cancellation at nominal magnitude three, selected by first background and fixed family and magnitude before comparison. Gray shading marks the disturbance. (a) Regional demand on observed support varies with the real background, while the injected change sums to zero in every group. (b) Positive and negative meter sets change locally. (c) Forecasts one hour ahead share target times and observed support, without assuming foreknowledge. (d) Affected probes change scores without crossing the acquisition gate during the event. The \DIFaddbeginFL \DIFaddFL {annotated }\DIFaddendFL later \DIFdelbeginFL \DIFdelFL {trigger }\DIFdelendFL \DIFaddbeginFL \DIFaddFL {spike occurs after the disturbance and }\DIFaddendFL also appears on the paired unmodified background. Acquisition remains unchanged and localization is missed. Local sets are evaluator labels unavailable to the policy}{figure.2}{}}
